dialect protocol
protocol stdio.stl.snapshot
version 1
schema stdio.stl
start body

# FG1: `stdio.stl` is TEXT-NATIVE for the `ArtifactPack` role — `encode_pack_with`/
# `decode_pack_with` (📸️snapshot/🦀️component.rs) wrap `encode_stl_ascii(self)`/`decode_stl_ascii`
# verbatim UTF-8 ASCII-STL text inside the SEMIO binary envelope (magic + token, described ONCE
# framework-side at `semio.envelope`'s own `.protocol.semio` per P2-M3, never re-described here).
# This is NOT the real, separate binary-STL byte layout the old placeholder described
# (`decode_stl_binary`/`encode_stl_binary`, ⚙️engine/component.rs:99-157) — that is a wholly
# different codec this artifact exposes only for cross-artifact export to `stdio.binary`
# (🚪️io/📤️export/…/💾️binary/🔖️raw/✳️any/🦀️component.rs's `serialize`), never reachable through
# `ArtifactPack`/this pack facet at all, so it is not honestly what THIS file describes.
#
# Model the bytes as if the walk already starts right after the envelope's token, matching every
# other text-native pilot (json's own worked §2.1 example, `🔣️json/…/📸️snapshot/💾️binary/📡️component.
# protocol.semio`) — cross-artifact `use semio.envelope` does not resolve at walk time yet (P2-M3).
# The payload itself is opaque, unstructured UTF-8 bytes at the BINARY layer by construction (its
# real internal grammar is `../📝️text/📖️component.grammar.semio`'s job, not the protocol dialect's) —
# `chain ... utf8` is the honest boundary.
framing record
chain payload utf8
